  "rationale": "Comparison for unit:given.typing.example.rejections against lean:Unique/TypingRejectionChecks:rejected_moves. rejected_moves universally excludes typings for known-empty and hidden left, exhibits an initialized hidden runtime field, permits partial-root transfer but rejects whole/constructor use, rejects hidden-field unpacking, and rejects the repeated constructor argument after the first move. This covers both static rejection and the contrasting dynamically possible cases described. Notation and judgment context was checked in unit:given.typing.example.views, unit:given.typing.expressions, unit:given.typing.bindings.",
